1
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:56,720
I made a deal for you to keep your ungrateful head

2
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:58,590
on your ungrateful neck a little while longer.

3
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:00,010
I'm sorry, what am I grateful for?

4
00:02:00,010 --> 00:02:02,040
The opportunity to live and die at the Wall

5
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,220
as punishment for a crime I did not commit?

6
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:06,080
You threw your life away. You threw it away.

7
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:08,670
It's not a joke. You understand that, don't you?

8
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:11,720
Of course it's a joke, just not a very funny one.

9
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,780
I couldn't.

10
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:18,150
I couldn't listen to her,

11
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,580
standing there telling her lies.

12
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:22,140
I couldn't do it.

13
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:24,870
You fell in love with a whore.

14
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:27,000
Yes, I fell in love with a whore.

15
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:31,020
And I was stupid enough to think that she had fallen in love with me.

16
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,750
That deal you made,

17
00:02:37,830 --> 00:02:40,020
it was everything Father wanted.

18
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:41,370
You do see that?

19
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:43,340
He gets you back as his heir.

20
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,600
The future Lord of the Rock.

21
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:48,070
And he ships me off to Castle Black,

22
00:02:48,070 --> 00:02:49,750
out of sight at last.

23
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:52,940
All so perfect.

24
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,940
It felt good to take that from him.

25
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:03,270
He knows I'm innocent and he's willing to sacrifice me anyway.

26
00:03:03,270 --> 00:03:05,130
He's willing to sacrifice any of us.

27
00:03:05,130 --> 00:03:06,390
Not you.

28
00:03:06,990 --> 00:03:08,710
You're the golden son.

29
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:11,290
You could kill a king, lose a hand,

30
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:13,890
fuck your own sister, you'll always be the golden son.

31
00:03:13,890 --> 00:03:14,920
Careful.

32
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:17,610
I'm the last friend you've got.

33
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:24,810
At least I got to tell them what they really are.

34
00:03:24,810 --> 00:03:26,910
Yes, brilliant speech.

35
00:03:26,990 --> 00:03:29,380
They'll be talking about it for days to come.

36
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:31,540
I thought you were a realist.

37
00:03:32,210 --> 00:03:34,440
Didn't realize you'd die for pride.

38
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,560
Don't give up on me just yet.

39
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,680
I survived one trial by combat,

40
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,600
even though you weren't there to save me.

41
00:03:41,610 --> 00:03:43,740
I can't save you this time either.

42
00:03:45,690 --> 00:03:47,670
My training has proved

43
00:03:47,670 --> 00:03:50,640
that I can't beat a stable boy with my left hand.

44
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,790
Where's your sense of adventure?

45
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:59,030
Even if you lose, imagine the look on Father's face when you fall.

46
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:02,800
Our family name snuffed out with a single swing of the sword.

47
00:04:04,130 --> 00:04:05,630
It is tempting.

48
00:04:23,430 --> 00:04:26,170
Bronn fought for me once, he'll do it again.

49
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:28,630
If he wins,

50
00:04:29,670 --> 00:04:33,060
I expect I'll be in his debt for the rest of my life.

51
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:34,950
If he wins.

52
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:36,600
Will you find him for me?

53
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:42,670
Who does Cersei plan on naming as a champion?

54
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:45,400
I hope it's Ser Meryn Trant.

55
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:49,120
I'd enjoy watching Bronn disembowel that pompous child beater.

56
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,850
No.

57
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:53,290
Not Ser Meryn.

58
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,070
Go on, move it.

59
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:06,630
And you.

60
00:05:07,830 --> 00:05:08,830
Come on.

61
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:19,600
Mercy.

62
00:05:21,330 --> 00:05:22,360
Please.

63
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:24,810
Please, mercy.

64
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:38,400
Ser Gregor. Welcome to the capital.

65
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,910
Thank you for riding here so quickly.

66
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,420
You seem to be in good form.

67
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:49,970
Who am I fighting?

68
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,090
Does it matter?

69
00:06:16,150 --> 00:06:17,600
Could be food.

70
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:19,600
Could be soldiers.

71
00:06:44,670 --> 00:06:46,660
You shouldn't be sitting out here like this.

72
00:06:47,350 --> 00:06:48,970
Where else to sit?

73
00:06:49,950 --> 00:06:51,990
Tried to walk back to my hut,

74
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,060
hurt too much.

75
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:57,930
Then I remembered they burned my hut down.

76
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,570
Who were "they"?

77
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:02,120
I stopped asking a while ago.

78
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:08,660
That's not gonna get better.

79
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,970
Doesn't seem so.

80
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,980
A bad way to go.

81
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:16,000
Haven't you had enough?

82
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:17,940
Of what?

83
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,360
I know.

84
00:07:23,250 --> 00:07:24,680
Time to go.

85
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:28,450
Take matters into my own hands.

86
00:07:30,330 --> 00:07:32,400
The thought has occurred to me.

87
00:07:36,710 --> 00:07:38,110
So why go on?

88
00:07:39,610 --> 00:07:40,680
Habit.

89
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:46,070
Nothing could be worse than this.

90
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:49,600
Maybe nothing is worse than this.

91
00:07:51,310 --> 00:07:55,420
Nothing isn't better or worse than anything.

92
00:07:58,110 --> 00:07:59,940
Nothing is just nothing.

93
00:08:05,270 --> 00:08:06,560
Who are you?

94
00:08:08,910 --> 00:08:10,250
My name is Arya.

95
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:13,040
Arya Stark.

96
00:08:16,570 --> 00:08:18,170
You her father?

97
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,270
Her captor.

98
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:23,750
Bringing her to her aunt for ransom.

99
00:08:24,780 --> 00:08:27,390
A fair exchange, that is.

100
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:34,670
Always held to the notion of fair exchange in all my dealings.

101
00:08:35,810 --> 00:08:39,490
You give me, I give you.

102
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,360
Fair.

103
00:08:42,770 --> 00:08:44,180
A balance.

104
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:48,520
No balance anymore.

105
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,980
Could I have a drink?

106
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:58,600
Dying is thirsty work.

107
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,820
Wish it were wine.

108
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,940
So do I.

109
00:09:32,810 --> 00:09:34,490
That's where the heart is.

110
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:40,120
That's how you kill a man.

111
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:49,580
The fuck you doing?

112
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:53,450
There's a price on your head.

113
00:09:53,570 --> 00:09:56,370
Guess that's what the king does when you tell him to fuck off.

114
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:58,160
The king's dead.

115
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:00,690
He drank poisoned wine at his own wedding.

116
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:03,770
The bounty on you is for killing Lannister soldiers.

117
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:05,550
100 silver stags.

118
00:10:05,550 --> 00:10:07,730
And you thought you were going to collect it?

119
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:09,830
Didn't think very hard, did you?

120
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:13,680
You were Yoren's prisoners when he was taking me to the Wall.

121
00:10:14,690 --> 00:10:17,890
He told me he'd fuck me bloody with a stick.

122
00:10:18,230 --> 00:10:21,280
This day's really not working out the way you planned.

123
00:10:21,330 --> 00:10:23,200
He on your little list?

124
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:25,230
He can't be.

125
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:27,900
I don't know his name.

126
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:30,930
What's your name?

127
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:35,170
-Rorge.  -Thank you.

128
00:10:41,510 --> 00:10:42,850
You're learning.

129
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:51,670
Rangers returning!

130
00:10:54,050 --> 00:10:55,280
They return!

131
00:10:56,590 --> 00:10:59,160
-Rangers returning!  -Greetings.

132
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,910
Didn't think I'd see you again.

133
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:01,980
All right, Jon?

134
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:03,880
Welcome back, brother.

135
00:11:12,870 --> 00:11:14,250
Lord Snow.

136
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:22,710
This is no place for wild beasts.

137
00:11:22,710 --> 00:11:24,100
Lock him away

138
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:26,840
or I'll let Hobb throw him in tonight's stew.

139
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,340
Come on, Ghost.

140
00:11:42,210 --> 00:11:45,720
Mance's army was closing in on Craster's Keep when we left.

141
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:48,590
We saw their campfires from Osric's Hill.

142
00:11:48,590 --> 00:11:50,650
They'll reach the Wall before the next full moon.

143
00:11:50,650 --> 00:11:52,670
I'm surprised you didn't ride over and say hello.

144
00:11:52,910 --> 00:11:55,370
The King-beyond-the-Wall is your old friend, isn't he?

145
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:56,710
We need to prepare.

146
00:11:56,710 --> 00:11:58,080
We've been preparing.

147
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,450
We should seal the tunnel.

148
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:03,110
Plug it with rocks and ice.

149
00:12:03,110 --> 00:12:04,480
Flood it and let it freeze.

150
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,080
And how would we range north?

151
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:07,940
-We wouldn't.  -Coward.

152
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:09,900
You would cut off our legs,

153
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:11,450
pluck out our eyes,

154
00:12:11,450 --> 00:12:13,290
leave us cowering behind the Wall

155
00:12:13,290 --> 00:12:15,210
hoping for the storm to pass?

156
00:12:15,210 --> 00:12:18,130
We can't defend the gate against 100,000 men.

157
00:12:18,130 --> 00:12:20,630
This castle has stood for thousands of years.

158
00:12:20,670 --> 00:12:23,800
The Night's Watch has defended her for thousands of years.

159
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:26,980
And in all those centuries, we have never sealed the tunnel.

160
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:29,140
Have you ever seen a giant, Ser Alliser?

161
00:12:30,170 --> 00:12:31,410
I have.

162
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,330
The tunnels, the gates won't stop them.

163
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:35,680
The bars on those gates are four inches thick.

164
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,080
Cold-rolled steel.

165
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:38,730
They won't stop them.

166
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:43,870
Remind me, which order you belong to, Lord Snow.

167
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:45,640
The stewards.

168
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:48,560
Are the stewards responsible for maintaining the tunnel?

169
00:12:49,910 --> 00:12:50,990
No.

170
00:12:51,090 --> 00:12:52,420
Who would that be?

171
00:12:54,470 --> 00:12:56,750
-The builders.  -Ah, the builders.

172
00:12:57,410 --> 00:12:59,090
First Builder Yarwyck,

173
00:12:59,090 --> 00:13:01,980
Lord Snow here recommends sealing the tunnel,

174
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:04,630
leaving us unable to carry out our duties

175
00:13:04,630 --> 00:13:07,100
as sworn brothers of the Night's Watch.

176
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:09,550
Do you agree with him?

177
00:13:18,770 --> 00:13:19,510
No.

178
00:13:21,570 --> 00:13:25,030
Given your deep knowledge of the wildling army, Lord Snow,

179
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:28,060
you and Tarly will take night duties atop the Wall

180
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:29,660
until the full moon.

181
00:13:32,830 --> 00:13:33,800
Moving on.

182
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:35,150
First Builder, we'll need

183
00:13:35,150 --> 00:13:37,890
100 barrels of pitch brought atop the wall.

184
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:04,320
My lord.

185
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:09,090
You have new clothes.

186
00:14:09,090 --> 00:14:11,170
Do you like 'em?

187
00:14:13,070 --> 00:14:14,400
Gloves are doeskin.

188
00:14:14,550 --> 00:14:16,000
Softer than a virgin's thighs.

189
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,790
I sent for you days ago.

190
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:20,020
-I've been a bit busy.  -Doing what?

191
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:25,830
My lonesome bachelor days are over.

192
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:29,860
I'm to wed Lollys Stokeworth.

193
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:33,730
Lollys Stokeworth?

194
00:14:33,930 --> 00:14:36,650
She doesn't strike me as your sort of girl.

195
00:14:37,630 --> 00:14:39,610
I wouldn't say I had a single sort of girl.

196
00:14:39,610 --> 00:14:40,990
She's dim-witted.

197
00:14:40,990 --> 00:14:42,580
If I wanted wits, I'd marry you.

198
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:46,160
When my sister arranged this love match,

199
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:49,220
did she mention that Lollys has an older sister?

200
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:50,190
Falyse.

201
00:14:50,750 --> 00:14:52,400
Aye, I did know about the older sister.

202
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:54,390
And you understand the rules of inheritance?

203
00:14:54,390 --> 00:14:56,010
Falyse is 40 and barren.

204
00:14:56,010 --> 00:14:59,360
She still gets Castle Stokeworth when her father dies.

205
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,300
She does.

206
00:15:00,710 --> 00:15:03,230
Unless she happens to perish before her father.

207
00:15:03,310 --> 00:15:04,940
Then Lollys gets the castle.

208
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:09,100
What? Ladies fall from their horses

209
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:11,110
and snap their pretty necks all the time.

210
00:15:11,170 --> 00:15:13,720
You and my sister deserve each other.

211
00:15:14,490 --> 00:15:16,700
Why did you bother to come here?

212
00:15:22,910 --> 00:15:26,450
You once said, if anyone ever asked me to sell you out,

213
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:27,930
you'd double their price.

214
00:15:27,930 --> 00:15:30,280
Is it two wives you want or two castles?

215
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:31,480
One of each will do.

216
00:15:32,710 --> 00:15:35,840
But if you want me to kill the Mountain for you,

217
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,410
it'd better be a damn big castle.

218
00:15:37,410 --> 00:15:39,690
I'm a bit short on castles at the moment.

219
00:15:39,690 --> 00:15:41,930
But I can offer you gold and gratitude.

220
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:43,070
I have gold.

221
00:15:43,570 --> 00:15:44,800
What can I buy with gratitude?

222
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,510
You might be surprised.

223
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:49,280
A Lannister always pays his debts.

224
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:50,760
Your sister's a Lannister, too.

225
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:53,280
My wife is heir to Winterfell.

226
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:57,150
If I emerge from this with my head still on my shoulders,

227
00:15:57,150 --> 00:16:00,490
I may one day rule the North in her name.

228
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:03,650
I could carve you out a big piece of it.

229
00:16:03,650 --> 00:16:05,440
If and may and could.

230
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:08,270
It's bloody cold up north.

231
00:16:08,390 --> 00:16:10,570
Lollys is soft and warm.

232
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:11,840
And close.

233
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:15,210
If I gave you the choice between fucking Lollys

234
00:16:15,210 --> 00:16:17,310
and fighting the Mountain, you'd have your britches down

235
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:19,090
and your cock out before I could blink.

236
00:16:19,090 --> 00:16:20,440
Does he frighten you so much?

237
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,430
I'd be a bloody fool if he didn't frighten me.

238
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,680
He's freakish big and freakish strong.

239
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:27,780
And quicker than you'd expect for a man of that size.

240
00:16:29,890 --> 00:16:31,370
Maybe I could take him,

241
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:33,240
dance around until he's so tired

242
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:35,220
of hacking at me, he dropped his sword,

243
00:16:35,230 --> 00:16:36,960
get him off his feet somehow.

244
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:39,480
But one misstep

245
00:16:39,570 --> 00:16:40,580
and I'm dead.

246
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:43,210
Why should I risk it?

247
00:16:44,330 --> 00:16:45,780
Because you're my friend.

248
00:16:45,790 --> 00:16:47,730
Aye, I'm your friend.

249
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,880
And when have you ever risked your life for me?

250
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,410
I like you,

251
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,790
pampered little shit that you are.

252
00:17:05,270 --> 00:17:07,150
I just like myself more.

253
00:17:07,150 --> 00:17:08,430
I understand.

254
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:10,340
I'm sorry it has to be this way.

255
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:11,890
Why are you sorry?

256
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,620
Because you're an evil bastard with no conscience and no heart?

257
00:17:16,620 --> 00:17:19,010
That's what I liked about you in the first place.

258
00:17:25,870 --> 00:17:27,350
We had some good days together.

259
00:17:27,350 --> 00:17:29,040
Yes, we did.

260
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:45,270
What will you do?

261
00:17:45,410 --> 00:17:49,250
I suppose I'll have to kill the Mountain myself.

262
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:52,780
Won't that make for a great song?

263
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:58,690
I hope to hear them sing it one day.

264
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,550
How did you get in here?

265
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:20,370
Your door is well guarded,

266
00:18:20,450 --> 00:18:21,830
but your window is not.

267
00:18:29,190 --> 00:18:32,230
I swam to an island a mile offshore for these.

268
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:34,750
Don't do that again.

269
00:18:36,250 --> 00:18:38,720
Never met a woman who didn't like wild flowers.

270
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,750
These are my private quarters.

271
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:43,800
If I want you here, I will summon you.

272
00:18:45,270 --> 00:18:48,130
Forgive me, my queen. I live to serve you.

273
00:18:54,310 --> 00:18:55,680
Tell me, why you're here?

274
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:01,640
I came to ask a favor.

275
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:04,650
I only have two talents in this world,

276
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:06,640
war and women.

277
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:09,670
You are staying here in Meereen to rule.

278
00:19:09,670 --> 00:19:11,570
That is a wise decision. I respect it.

279
00:19:11,570 --> 00:19:13,840
But here in Meereen, I cannot pursue my talents.

280
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:16,430
I've ordered the Second Sons to patrol the streets

281
00:19:16,430 --> 00:19:17,850
to stop the revenge killing.

282
00:19:17,850 --> 00:19:19,050
You've ordered us to be night watchmen.

283
00:19:19,050 --> 00:19:20,910
And as for women,

284
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:25,270
there are thousands in Meereen you can pursue.

285
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:27,240
There is only one,

286
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:29,740
and she does not want me.

287
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:33,040
You swore me your sword.

288
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:35,850
My sword is yours till the day I die.

289
00:19:35,850 --> 00:19:38,110
So if I command you to stay in Meereen

290
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:39,610
and patrol the streets?

291
00:19:39,610 --> 00:19:41,680
I'll stay in Meereen and patrol the streets.

292
00:19:43,110 --> 00:19:44,970
Send me to kill your enemies.

293
00:19:44,980 --> 00:19:47,130
Any enemy, anywhere.

294
00:19:48,550 --> 00:19:50,150
Let me do what I do best.

295
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:53,440
Very well.

296
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:01,930
Do what you do best.

297
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:15,030
Take off your clothes.

298
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:49,390
Come in, my queen. Please.

299
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:51,170
I didn't mean to disturb you, my lady.

300
00:20:51,170 --> 00:20:52,490
You could never disturb me.

301
00:20:52,490 --> 00:20:55,150
I just wanted to speak with you before we left.

302
00:20:55,910 --> 00:20:57,810
Could you bring me that vial over there?

303
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:01,950
The blue one.

304
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:06,280
No, no, no. Not that one.

305
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:09,090
You don't even want to touch that one.

306
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:10,210
Next to it.

307
00:21:12,230 --> 00:21:13,320
That's the one.

308
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:34,320
When I looked into the flames this morning,

309
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:35,800
the Lord spoke to me.

310
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:37,330
He said,

311
00:21:38,530 --> 00:21:43,030
"Tonight, you will have your last good bath in a long while.

312
00:21:43,670 --> 00:21:44,760
Make it count."

313
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:49,930
A joke.

314
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:53,360
Not a very good one, I'm afraid.

315
00:21:53,430 --> 00:21:54,730
It was.

316
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,390
I humor isn't my strength.

317
00:21:57,860 --> 00:22:00,000
That's because most jokes are lies

318
00:22:00,620 --> 00:22:02,600
and you're devoted to the truth.

319
00:22:02,710 --> 00:22:05,440
If they're lies, my lady, aren't they best avoided?

320
00:22:05,970 --> 00:22:07,200
Not always.

321
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:19,970
Most of these powders and potions

322
00:22:20,890 --> 00:22:21,830
are lies.

323
00:22:21,830 --> 00:22:25,250
Deceptions to make men think they witnessed our Lord's power.

324
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:27,710
Once they step into his light,

325
00:22:27,710 --> 00:22:29,610
they will see the lie for what it was.

326
00:22:30,130 --> 00:22:32,410
The trick that led them to the truth.

327
00:22:33,210 --> 00:22:35,250
A pinch of this powder in a bonfire

328
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:39,150
will send a flaming column screaming towards the sky.

329
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:41,850
And this one creates a black smoke

330
00:22:41,850 --> 00:22:44,550
that will make the bravest man piss himself with fear.

331
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:47,610
And a drop of this in any man's wine

332
00:22:47,620 --> 00:22:50,040
will drive him wild with lust.

333
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:55,460
Did you use it with Stannis?

334
00:22:55,590 --> 00:22:56,370
No.

335
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:01,360
Don't be upset.

336
00:23:01,610 --> 00:23:04,120
Men never crave what they already have.

337
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:07,900
It's only flesh.

338
00:23:08,950 --> 00:23:10,680
It needs what it needs.

339
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:17,380
No act done in service of the Lord

340
00:23:17,790 --> 00:23:19,770
can ever be called a sin.

341
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:23,380
I thank God every day for bringing you to us.

342
00:23:23,830 --> 00:23:25,380
And Stannis to you.

343
00:23:26,610 --> 00:23:30,510
He wants to bring Shireen with us.

344
00:23:31,630 --> 00:23:34,790
I think that would be ill-advised.

345
00:23:35,170 --> 00:23:39,000
My daughter has heretical tendencies, as you're well aware.

346
00:23:39,050 --> 00:23:42,380
I don't know if her doubt is real or simply meant to spite me,

347
00:23:42,380 --> 00:23:46,130
but whichever the case, she should stay home.

348
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:52,510
I understand how you feel.

349
00:23:53,860 --> 00:23:55,300
But that is impossible.

350
00:23:59,050 --> 00:23:59,990
Why?

351
00:24:02,050 --> 00:24:04,610
You don't need powders and potions, my queen.

352
00:24:05,240 --> 00:24:06,660
You don't need lies.

353
00:24:07,730 --> 00:24:10,300
You are strong enough to look into the Lord's light

354
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:12,420
and see his truth for yourself.

355
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,100
However harsh it is.

356
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:23,000
However hard for us to understand.

357
00:24:24,470 --> 00:24:26,080
You don't need my help,

358
00:24:26,210 --> 00:24:28,140
but I will need yours soon.

359
00:24:28,980 --> 00:24:31,640
When we set sail, your daughter must be with us.

360
00:24:35,850 --> 00:24:37,130
The Lord needs her.

361
00:24:45,890 --> 00:24:47,260
Jorah the Andal.

362
00:24:48,990 --> 00:24:50,720
Are you here to see our queen?

363
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:54,130
She's in a good mood.

364
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:10,660
Khaleesi.

365
00:25:11,630 --> 00:25:14,160
-You're here early.  -Later than some.

366
00:25:16,450 --> 00:25:17,800
You don't approve?

367
00:25:17,800 --> 00:25:20,390
It's not a question of approval, it's a question of trust.

368
00:25:20,390 --> 00:25:22,390
You neither approve nor trust.

369
00:25:22,390 --> 00:25:24,240
Why would I? The man's a sellsword.

370
00:25:24,240 --> 00:25:25,550
Didn't you fight for the Golden Company

371
00:25:25,550 --> 00:25:27,430
before pledging your sword to my brother?

372
00:25:27,900 --> 00:25:28,790
I did.

373
00:25:29,380 --> 00:25:30,650
I trust you.

374
00:25:30,650 --> 00:25:34,100
Daario Naharis killed his captains and dumped their heads at your feet

375
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:36,400
when he grew tired of their commands.

376
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,240
How could you ever have faith in a man like that?

377
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:41,330
I could never have faith in a man like Daario.

378
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:46,550
That's why I've sent him and the Second Sons to retake Yunkai.

379
00:25:48,850 --> 00:25:50,630
-You have?  -I have.

380
00:25:50,630 --> 00:25:52,520
Without you there to rule, Khaleesi,

381
00:25:52,530 --> 00:25:54,940
I fear the masters will simply bide their time,

382
00:25:54,940 --> 00:25:57,300
wait for the invaders to leave and reassert control.

383
00:25:57,310 --> 00:25:58,780
That is why I've ordered Daario

384
00:25:58,780 --> 00:26:01,750
to execute every master in Yunkai.

385
00:26:02,830 --> 00:26:05,500
The masters tear babies from their mothers' arms.

386
00:26:05,500 --> 00:26:07,840
They mutilate little boys by the thousands.

387
00:26:07,860 --> 00:26:10,460
They train little girls in the art of pleasuring old men.

388
00:26:10,460 --> 00:26:13,530
They treat men like beasts, as you said yourself.

389
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:14,880
Herding the masters into

390
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:17,030
pens and slaughtering them by the thousands

391
00:26:17,030 --> 00:26:19,210
is also treating men like beasts.

392
00:26:19,450 --> 00:26:21,100
The slaves you freed,

393
00:26:21,450 --> 00:26:23,660
brutality is all they've ever known.

394
00:26:23,670 --> 00:26:25,720
If you want them to know something else,

395
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:27,170
you'll have to show it to them.

396
00:26:27,170 --> 00:26:29,110
And repay the slavers with what? Kindness?

397
00:26:29,110 --> 00:26:30,800
A fine? A stern warning?

398
00:26:30,800 --> 00:26:33,740
It's tempting to see your enemies as evil, all of them,

399
00:26:33,740 --> 00:26:36,380
but there's good and evil on both sides in every war ever fought.

400
00:26:36,380 --> 00:26:38,970
Let the priests argue over good and evil.

401
00:26:38,970 --> 00:26:40,820
Slavery is real.

402
00:26:40,890 --> 00:26:42,760
I can end it. I will end it.

403
00:26:42,760 --> 00:26:45,450
And I will end those behind it.

404
00:26:45,450 --> 00:26:47,640
I sold men into slavery, Khaleesi.

405
00:26:47,840 --> 00:26:52,730
And now, you are helping me show them to freedom.

406
00:26:53,140 --> 00:26:55,480
I wouldn't be here to help you if Ned Stark had done to me

407
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:57,700
what you want to do to the masters of Yunkai.

408
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:06,220
The man who came to me the other day about burying his father.

409
00:27:06,430 --> 00:27:08,280
Hizdahr zo Loraq?

410
00:27:09,520 --> 00:27:11,000
He will accompany the Second Sons

411
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:13,110
and serve as my ambassador to Yunkai.

412
00:27:13,260 --> 00:27:15,980
He will tell the masters what has happened in Meereen.

413
00:27:16,100 --> 00:27:19,620
He will explain the choice they have before them.

414
00:27:19,660 --> 00:27:21,600
They can live in my new world

415
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:24,520
or they can die in their old one.

416
00:27:28,970 --> 00:27:31,240
Well, go and catch Daario before he leaves.

417
00:27:31,690 --> 00:27:33,240
Tell him, I changed my mind.

418
00:27:34,070 --> 00:27:35,420
Yes, Khaleesi.

419
00:27:41,150 --> 00:27:41,980
No.

420
00:27:45,970 --> 00:27:47,860
Tell him you changed my mind.

421
00:28:00,070 --> 00:28:01,590
Rat cunts.

422
00:28:03,860 --> 00:28:05,020
Fucking whore.

423
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:08,740
You're doing it wrong.

424
00:28:10,130 --> 00:28:12,210
You need to burn away that horrible bit there.

425
00:28:12,510 --> 00:28:14,590
Otherwise it's gonna get infected and fester.

426
00:28:17,520 --> 00:28:20,130
I know you don't like fire, but if you don't do it right.

427
00:28:20,130 --> 00:28:21,300
No fire.

428
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:24,720
It'll only take a second.

429
00:28:25,510 --> 00:28:27,380
-It won't hurt that much.  -No fire!

430
00:28:42,530 --> 00:28:43,880
Shut up about it.

431
00:28:47,450 --> 00:28:49,060
Shut up about everything.

432
00:28:49,740 --> 00:28:51,920
Thanks to you, I'm a walking bag of silver

433
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:53,710
anywhere the Lannisters hold sway.

434
00:28:55,890 --> 00:28:57,720
Which is everywhere between where we are now

435
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:59,100
and where we're going.

436
00:29:01,830 --> 00:29:04,520
I'm as stupid as that hog you stuck back in the village,

437
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:09,830
getting myself cut and stabbed and bitten.

438
00:29:12,730 --> 00:29:14,810
No reward is worth this much trouble.

439
00:29:15,580 --> 00:29:17,110
Wish I'd never laid eyes on you.

440
00:29:28,220 --> 00:29:30,610
You say your brother gave you that sword.

441
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:34,790
My brother gave me this.

442
00:29:37,170 --> 00:29:39,480
It was just like you said a while back.

443
00:29:40,310 --> 00:29:41,410
Pressed me to the fire

444
00:29:41,410 --> 00:29:44,180
like I was a nice juicy mutton chop.

445
00:29:48,460 --> 00:29:49,330
Why?

446
00:29:49,460 --> 00:29:50,930
Thought I stole one of his toys.

447
00:29:50,930 --> 00:29:53,280
I didn't steal it. I was just playing with it.

448
00:29:58,740 --> 00:29:59,930
The pain was bad.

449
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:02,570
The smell was worse.

450
00:30:06,300 --> 00:30:09,690
But the worst thing was that it was my brother who did it.

451
00:30:14,330 --> 00:30:16,480
My father, who protected him

452
00:30:19,310 --> 00:30:21,560
told everyone my bedding caught fire.

453
00:30:34,690 --> 00:30:36,290
You think you're on your own?

454
00:30:39,870 --> 00:30:41,090
Let me wash it out

455
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:43,390
and help you sew it up at least.

456
00:31:10,450 --> 00:31:12,120
Bit of comfort never hurt anyone.

457
00:31:12,540 --> 00:31:14,760
We've been sleeping in ditches the last few weeks.

458
00:31:14,900 --> 00:31:17,570
I think we can treat ourselves to a featherbed for the night

459
00:31:18,010 --> 00:31:20,010
and a hot meal not cooked by you.

460
00:31:20,030 --> 00:31:21,610
Couldn't agree more, my lady.

461
00:31:21,610 --> 00:31:23,970
Just don't start expecting silk underclothes.

462
00:31:24,270 --> 00:31:26,170
Not working for your former lord any longer.

463
00:31:26,170 --> 00:31:28,380
-Yes, my lady.  -Don't get drunk.

464
00:31:30,580 --> 00:31:31,550
No, my lady.

465
00:31:31,550 --> 00:31:32,800
Can I get you anything else?

466
00:31:32,830 --> 00:31:34,580
No, this will do nicely, thank you.

467
00:31:34,820 --> 00:31:36,400
Kidney pie is wonderful.

468
00:31:36,750 --> 00:31:37,730
Thanks.

469
00:31:38,970 --> 00:31:40,130
I do my best.

470
00:31:42,340 --> 00:31:44,700
A good kidney pie is all about the ingredients.

471
00:31:44,710 --> 00:31:47,460
Flour, lard, water, eggs, milk.

472
00:31:47,790 --> 00:31:49,590
Easy enough. But the meat,

473
00:31:49,590 --> 00:31:52,350
peacetime or not, getting your hands on a good bottom round steak

474
00:31:52,350 --> 00:31:54,350
and calves' kidneys is not easy.

475
00:31:54,360 --> 00:31:56,580
I mean, some people settle for plain old beef kidneys.

476
00:31:57,370 --> 00:31:58,970
Got no right to cook anything, them.

477
00:31:58,990 --> 00:32:00,280
Oh, and the gravy.

478
00:32:00,620 --> 00:32:02,460
Don't get me started on the gravy.

479
00:32:02,460 --> 00:32:04,070
Very difficult to get right.

480
00:32:04,070 --> 00:32:05,630
See, a lot of people give up on the gravy.

481
00:32:05,630 --> 00:32:07,960
You cannot give up on the gravy.

482
00:32:08,140 --> 00:32:10,010
No gravy, no pie.

483
00:32:10,010 --> 00:32:11,210
Simple as that.

484
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:15,490
That's nice armor. Are you a knight?

485
00:32:17,710 --> 00:32:18,610
No.

486
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:22,520
Oh, it's just people with armor are usually knights.

487
00:32:22,550 --> 00:32:24,930
Generally speaking. From King's Landing, though, aren't you?

488
00:32:24,930 --> 00:32:27,740
From there myself originally. Flea Bottom born and bred.

489
00:32:27,930 --> 00:32:29,570
What brings you to these parts?

490
00:32:30,820 --> 00:32:32,130
We're looking for someone.

491
00:32:32,130 --> 00:32:34,130
Someone in particular? Maybe they came in here.

492
00:32:34,130 --> 00:32:36,560
A lot of people come in here. Just the other day we had 17.

493
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:38,660
A girl, tall, red hair, very pretty.

494
00:32:38,660 --> 00:32:41,570
Her name is Sansa Stark, but she may be using a different name.

495
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:43,820
Starks?

496
00:32:47,620 --> 00:32:49,860
What, like them lot from "Winterhell"?

497
00:32:53,660 --> 00:32:55,580
No, ain't seen anyone like that.

498
00:32:56,010 --> 00:32:57,490
I heard they was all traitors.

499
00:32:58,290 --> 00:32:59,760
Don't need no traitors in here.

500
00:32:59,760 --> 00:33:02,310
I pledged my life to their mother Catelyn Stark.

501
00:33:02,830 --> 00:33:05,040
I swore to her I'd bring her daughters home.

502
00:33:10,050 --> 00:33:11,950
Sure I can't get you a bit more kidney pie?

503
00:33:26,820 --> 00:33:27,750
What?

504
00:33:27,990 --> 00:33:29,350
It's nothing, my lady.

505
00:33:29,940 --> 00:33:32,600
You wouldn't be screwing your face up like that if it was nothing.

506
00:33:32,740 --> 00:33:34,940
Don't want to offend, my lady. Truly, I don't.

507
00:33:34,940 --> 00:33:36,830
You're not interesting enough to be offensive.

508
00:33:38,780 --> 00:33:40,900
The Lannisters want Lady Sansa.

509
00:33:41,480 --> 00:33:43,050
The Lannisters have money.

510
00:33:43,680 --> 00:33:45,390
People kill for money.

511
00:33:46,830 --> 00:33:48,380
I don't think we should be telling people,

512
00:33:48,380 --> 00:33:50,230
we're searching for Lady Sansa.

513
00:33:59,660 --> 00:34:03,030
My lady. My lord. Could I have a word?

514
00:34:03,040 --> 00:34:04,970
What about? Not kidney pie.

515
00:34:05,070 --> 00:34:06,690
You seem like a proper lady.

516
00:34:06,890 --> 00:34:08,510
Someone who could be trusted.

517
00:34:10,730 --> 00:34:12,490
I never met no Sansa Stark.

518
00:34:13,580 --> 00:34:15,040
But I know her sister.

519
00:34:16,010 --> 00:34:17,240
Arya.

520
00:34:19,820 --> 00:34:21,250
No one's seen Arya Stark

521
00:34:21,250 --> 00:34:23,020
since her father was beheaded.

522
00:34:23,270 --> 00:34:24,720
She's presumed dead.

523
00:34:25,690 --> 00:34:27,520
She weren't when I last spoke to her.

524
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:29,900
-When was that?  -Heading up north with the Night's Watch.

525
00:34:29,900 --> 00:34:31,420
She was all dressed up as a boy.

526
00:34:31,820 --> 00:34:34,140
Like your ladyship, only without the armor.

527
00:34:34,330 --> 00:34:35,780
Going by the name Arry.

528
00:34:36,190 --> 00:34:37,890
-So what happened to her?  -Well.

529
00:34:37,890 --> 00:34:39,200
The quick version.

530
00:34:40,550 --> 00:34:42,150
The Lannisters took us prisoner.

531
00:34:43,070 --> 00:34:44,280
We escaped.

532
00:34:44,880 --> 00:34:46,380
The Brotherhood took us prisoner.

533
00:34:46,380 --> 00:34:48,120
They sold me to the innkeep.

534
00:34:48,300 --> 00:34:50,410
They were gonna sell Arya to her mother at Riverrun

535
00:34:50,410 --> 00:34:51,740
along with another prisoner.

536
00:34:51,740 --> 00:34:53,580
Big ugly fellow. Foul mouth

537
00:34:53,580 --> 00:34:55,180
and a face like a half-burnt ham.

538
00:34:55,540 --> 00:34:57,540
-Not friendly.  -The Hound.

539
00:34:57,850 --> 00:34:59,080
That's the one.

540
00:34:59,810 --> 00:35:02,980
